{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"39","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Company Income Growth"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"64 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Petya works as a PR manager for a successful Berland company BerSoft. He needs to prepare a presentation on the company income growth since "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2001"},{"kind":"text","text":" (the year of its founding) till now. Petya knows that in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2001"},{"kind":"text","text":" the company income amounted to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a1"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion bourles, in "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2002"},{"kind":"text","text":" — to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a2"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion, ..., and in the current "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2000 + n)"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th year — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"an"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion bourles. On the base of the information Petya decided to show in his presentation the linear progress history which is in his opinion perfect. According to a graph Petya has already made, in the first year BerSoft company income must amount to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion bourles, in the second year — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion bourles etc., each following year the income increases by "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion bourles. Unfortunately, the real numbers are different from the perfect ones. Among the numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" can even occur negative ones that are a sign of the company’s losses in some years. That is why Petya wants to ignore some data, in other words, cross some numbers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" from the sequence and leave only some subsequence that has perfect growth."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus Petya has to choose a sequence of years "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y2"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yk"},{"kind":"text","text":",so that in the year "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1"},{"kind":"text","text":" the company income amounted to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion bourles, in the year "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y2"},{"kind":"text","text":" — "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"2"},{"kind":"text","text":" billion bourles etc., in accordance with the perfect growth dynamics. Help him to choose the longest such sequence."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains an integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The next line contains "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":" - 100 ≤ ai ≤ 100"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"ai"},{"kind":"text","text":" determines the income of BerSoft company in the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(2000 + i)"},{"kind":"text","text":"-th year. The numbers in the line are separated by spaces."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" — the maximum possible length of a perfect sequence. In the next line output the sequence of years "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y1"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"y2"},{"kind":"text","text":", ..., "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"yk"},{"kind":"text","text":". Separate the numbers by spaces. If the answer is not unique, output any. If no solution exist, output one number "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"0"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"10\n-2 1 1 3 2 3 4 -10 -2 5\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\n2002 2005 2006 2007 2010\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n-1 -2 -3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"39B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/39/problem/B"}